[ISSUE #1]
WebSocket Connection Failure

Description:
WebSocket connection failed when accessing the application
through private IP addresses on both the host machine and
other devices.

Symptom:
HTTP, CSS, and JavaScript loaded successfully, but the
WebSocket connection was never initiated.

Cause:
crypto.randomUUID() was not supported in the browser
environment, causing JavaScript execution to stop before
the WebSocket connection was created.

Fix:
Replaced crypto.randomUUID() with a base-36 client ID
generated using Date.now() and Math.random().

Secondary Fix:
Updated client ID regex patterns from [a-f0-9-]+ to [a-z0-9]+
to support the new client ID format.

Result:
WebSocket connections now work correctly through private
IP addresses and across devices on the same network.